---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Philosophy"
  description="The editorial position and publishing principles of Independent Web Almanac."
>
  <SectionHeader
    eyebrow="Standards"
    title="Craft matters more than workflow theater."
    description="IWA is interested in meaningful human-guided creative work, not in turning process into a purity test."
  />

  <section class="page-copy">
    <p>
      Modern creative tools are part of the landscape. IWA does not treat
      AI-assisted work as something shameful, exotic, or automatically suspect.
      It is allowed. It is normal. It is also not a substitute for judgment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Authors may disclose process details when they are relevant, useful, or
      personally important. Disclosure is not required as a standing condition
      of publication. The editorial standard is the finished work and the
      human responsibility behind it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The publication avoids hype, panic, and argument for its own sake. It
      focuses on craft, quality, structure, usefulness, reader experience, and
      the practical realities of publishing in the modern era.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
